   351	What it does:
   352	  Refreshes the framework-derived content (team.md, skills/, hooks/,
   353	  scripts/, commands/, pitfalls-catalog.yaml, task-chains.yaml, the
   354	  SPEC/v1 contract (forced route, skipped on --ceremony user installs)
   355	  and the .claude/.framework-version marker) in an existing adopter
   356	  install. User-customized files (CLAUDE.md, MEMORY.md,
   357	  .claude/agent-metrics.md) are NOT touched, and the root VERSION file
   358	  is NEVER touched (install-time snapshot — ADR-155-AMEND-1; read
   359	  .claude/.framework-version for the installed framework version). NOTE: .claude/settings.json IS
   360	  updated in place by the default-on baseline migration (the model/permission
   361	  leaf keys: model, availableModels, fallbackModel, permissions.defaultMode)
   362	  and the idempotent settings-merge (new lifecycle-hook registrations) —
   363	  adopter-CUSTOMIZED values are always preserved with a named warning, and a
   364	  pre-migration backup is written to .claude.bak/. Opt out with
   365	  --no-settings-migrate / --no-settings-merge to manage settings.json by hand.
   366	
   367	Options:
   368	  --profile <list>      Comma-separated profiles to refresh (default: core,frontend).
   369	                        Available: core, frontend, <domain-name>.
   370	                        Example: --profile core,fintech
   371	  --stack <name>        Stack-specific hooks override (default: none).
   372	                        Example: --stack node
   373	  --pin <tag>           Pin source to specific tag/SHA (SPEC v1 install-cli.md).
   374	                        Refuses if target has uncommitted .claude/ changes.
   375	                        Example: --pin v1.18.0
   376	  --dry-run             Print what WOULD be replaced without modifying $TARGET.
   377	  --no-diff-warn        Silence the F-CHAOS-3 "customization will be replaced" warnings.
   378	  --no-deprecation-warn Silence the PLAN-135 advisory model-deprecation scan
   379	                        (the scan never blocks the upgrade either way).
   380	  --no-settings-merge   Skip the PLAN-135 W2 idempotent settings-merge step
   381	                        that registers new lifecycle hooks (e.g. the Setup
   382	                        post-install self-verification hook) into the adopter's
   383	                        existing .claude/settings.json. The merge is idempotent
   384	                        + fail-open (never blocks the upgrade); pass this to opt
   385	                        out entirely and manage settings.json by hand.
   386	  --no-settings-migrate PLAN-163 T5.4: skip the baseline-aware settings
   387	                        migration (model, availableModels, fallbackModel,
   388	                        permissions.defaultMode + T3.4-gated new-event
   389	                        registrations). 3-state policy per LEAF KEY:
   390	                        absent -> write the new baseline; equal to the OLD
   391	                        baseline (byte-compared) -> update; customized ->
   392	                        PRESERVE + named WARNING. Idempotent + fail-open;
   393	                        never blocks the upgrade.
   394	  --settings-migrate-only
   395	                        Run ONLY the T5.4 settings baseline migration
   396	                        against <target-repo-path> and exit 0 (test/ops
   397	                        seam; honors --dry-run + --no-settings-migrate).
   398	  --print-settings-baselines
   399	                        Print the normative T5.4 baseline table (JSON) and
   400	                        exit 0. Oracles derive their expectations from this
   401	                        output instead of hardcoding the literals.
   402	  --no-replay           PLAN-153 Wave B (B2): do NOT replay the recorded
   403	                        install request from .claude/.install-state.json.
   404	                        By default, when that file exists and validates,
   405	                        --profile/--stack DEFAULT to the recorded values
